Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:39:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 536/536] Entrypoints: the SageMaker routes' import leaves the
 root logging as it was

model_hosting_container_standards sets the root logger to
SAGEMAKER_CONTAINER_LOG_LEVEL (else LOG_LEVEL, else ERROR) and raises every
root handler below that level to it, when it is first imported. The API
server imports it for the SageMaker routes, so with neither variable set,
vllm serve's log dropped every third-party warning that propagates to the
root logger (vLLM's own loggers have their own handler).

vllm.entrypoints.serve.sagemaker.standards imports it for both routers and
puts the root logger's level and its handlers' levels back, unless one of the
two variables is set, which keeps the library's documented behavior. The
routes are unchanged.

Test: in a fresh interpreter, a third-party warning reaches a root handler
after the server's imports, with the root levels unchanged; with
SAGEMAKER_CONTAINER_LOG_LEVEL=ERROR the library's level applies.
